-- title:
--   No commuting representation shares the character of a 2-dimensional Burnside representation
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field, $G$ a monoid, and $V$, $V'$ finite-dimensional $k$-vector spaces, with $\dim_k V = 2$. Let $\rho : G \to \operatorname{End}_k(V)$ be a monoid homomorphism whose image spans $\operatorname{End}_k(V)$ as a $k$-vector space, i.e. the $k$-submodule generated by the set $\rho(G)$ is the whole endomorphism algebra, and let $\tau : G \to \operatorname{End}_k(V')$ be a monoid homomorphism whose values pairwise commute, $\tau(g)\tau(h) = \tau(h)\tau(g)$ for all $g, h \in G$. Assume furthermore that $\rho$ and $\tau$ have the same character, in the sense that $\operatorname{tr}_{k,V}(\rho(g)) = \operatorname{tr}_{k,V'}(\tau(g))$ for every $g \in G$. Then these hypotheses are contradictory: the conclusion is `False`. No relation between $\dim_k V'$ and $2$ is assumed, and $\tau$ is not assumed to span anything; the statement is thus the assertion that a two-dimensional representation satisfying Burnside's spanning condition cannot have the same trace function as any representation with commuting image.
--
--   This is the elementary substitute for Brauer–Nesbitt used to rule out that an absolutely irreducible two-dimensional residual representation has the character of a sum of characters (the "non-Eisenstein" condition), the spanning hypothesis being Burnside's form of absolute irreducibility. It is invoked in the Taylor–Wiles level analysis, in the arguments establishing unipotence on inertia and the existence of a basis on which inertia acts by diamond operators.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Representation_false_of_span_eq_top_of_trace_eq_of_commute.lean

import Mathlib.Algebra.MonoidAlgebra.Basic
import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Trace
import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.Free

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem Representation.false_of_span_eq_top_of_trace_eq_of_commute
    {k G V V' : Type*} [Field k] [Monoid G]
    [AddCommGroup V] [Module k V] [FiniteDimensional k V]
    [AddCommGroup V'] [Module k V'] [FiniteDimensional k V']
    (h2 : Module.finrank k V = 2)
    (ρ : G →* Module.End k V) (hspan : Submodule.span k (Set.range ρ) = ⊤)
    (τ : G →* Module.End k V') (hcomm : ∀ g h : G, Commute (τ g) (τ h))
    (htr : ∀ g : G, LinearMap.trace k V (ρ g) = LinearMap.trace k V' (τ g)) : False := by sorry
